strings |id, value|

bug_descriptions |bug_id, line_num, content|
    web_render_k1_lead_space_run_start_tie_2026-11-28, 0, "At device scale 1 a text run that opens with a collapsible space after an inline element (`<code>x</code> — partial`) lands on Chrome's whole px only when the lead space is charged as its LayoutUnit-ceiled advance (PR #12215). With the exact advance, which is what Chrome's item model gives the run's own glyphs and what matches Chrome at k=4 (inline_lead_space_run_pen_phase_k4_chrome159_spec), the 1x catalog rises: html 0.30 -> 0.36, css-layout 0.41 -> 0.42, css-paint 0.41 -> 0.44, animation 0.37 -> 0.41 (seed1126b, base 531e49cc972). So the k=1 run start has a separate rounding-tie error that the 1/64 px nudge hides: the pen is a sum of milli-rounded advances and lands just below ties Chrome rounds up (same limit named in inline_run_start_quarter_phase_k4_chrome159_spec, RUN n=4 and n=12). The engine keeps the snapped lead at k == 1 as a measured workaround; the real fix is exact (font-unit) pen origins or Chrome's k=1 run-start rounding rule, after which the k == 1 branch can go."

bugs_active |id, severity, status, title, file, line, reproducible_by, created_at, updated_at, valid|
    web_render_k1_lead_space_run_start_tie_2026-11-28, P3, fix-implemented-verification-pending, "web render: at k=1 a lead-space run needs the LayoutUnit-snapped space to hit Chrome's whole px; the exact advance loses rounding ties", src/lib/gc_async_mut/gpu/browser_engine/simple_web_html_layout_renderer_layout_engine.spl, 5075, "1x catalog (scripts/check/check-chrome-catalog-pixel-diff.shs) with the k == 1 branch of lead_milli set to lead_exact_milli", -11-28, true

bug_investigation_logs |bug_id, line_num, content|
    web_render_k1_lead_space_run_start_tie_2026-11-28, 0, "2026-11-28 anim-regress lane: exact lead at every scale (commit e967fc01b40) gave 4x animation 18267 -> 15997 px but 1x html 0.30 -> 0.36; gating the exact lead on k > 1 (04b14b375ce) made all eight 1x frames byte-identical to base. No Chrome 1x per-run measurement was taken; which rows flip at 1x is not yet known."

    web_render_k1_lead_space_run_start_tie_2026-11-28, 1, "2026-11-28 1x-lcd lane (work/webrender-1x-lcd-20261128): root cause was pen drift, not the lead. LCD pens were sums of milli-rounded advances and came out a few milli short of a quarter tie about ten glyphs into a run; the snapped lead (+1/128 px at 16 px) hid that on the lines whose preceding item is an odd number of 1/128 px wide. With pens as exact unit sums (lcd_quarter_phase_long_run_chrome159_spec) the 1x catalog on 8b2da8a67a1 measures 13,762 mismatching px with the exact lead at k=1 and 14,275 with the snapped lead (forms-media 0.34 vs 0.42, css-paint 0.35 vs 0.40; html 0.29 vs 0.27, css-layout 0.40 vs 0.37, animation 0.34 vs 0.32), so the k == 1 branch now takes lead_exact_milli. Neither is right on every line until the item before the run is ceiled to a LayoutUnit: bug web_render_inline_item_layoutunit_ceil_pen_2026-11-28."
